//! The navi standard library.
//!
//! Module paths, type names, trait names and method signatures follow Rust's
//! std; deviations are listed in spec/std-diff.md. Beyond Rust's std it
//! has what Go's standard library has (networking, HTTP, TLS, crypto,
//! encodings, compression, time zones, command lines): those modules'
//! APIs follow the Rust crates people use for them.

